@startuml People and Access Use Cases

title Use cases: volunteers, logins and access
caption Target design. Decisions O34, O35, O19, X12, O14, O31. ADRs 0010, 0017.

left to right direction

actor "Volunteer\n(any role)" as vol
actor Administrator as admin
actor "Identity provider" as idp <<system>>

rectangle "Freedom" {
  usecase "Sign in" as A1
  usecase "See who I am (/me)" as A2
  usecase "Approve a volunteer" as A3
  usecase "Link a login to a person" as A4
  usecase "Grant roles\n(via the identity provider)" as A5
  usecase "Assign a Loader to locations" as A6
  usecase "Erase a volunteer" as A7
  usecase "Make a change\n(recorded as theirs)" as A8
}

vol --> A1
vol --> A2
vol --> A8
admin --> A3
admin --> A4
admin --> A5
admin --> A6
admin --> A7
A1 ..> idp
A5 ..> idp

note right of A8
  Refused (403) for a login not linked
  to a person (O35). Every change records
  who made it and when (O19).
end note

note right of A7
  Deletes personal details and the login link.
  Refused while the volunteer is still needed.
  Records that name them read "Former volunteer".
end note

@enduml
